# Read from the CONTEXT ROOT, which is this directory — the SPA build needs the workspace's
# manifests, so it cannot be scoped to apps/portal/.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE FALLBACK, NOT THE ONLY ONE. BuildKit reads `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore`
# when one exists beside the Dockerfile, and only falls back here otherwise. `apps/portal/` has no
# such file, so the SPA build reads this one — which is what the `lambdas` and `infra` exclusions
# below are for, and what the SPA build's own `test ! -d lambdas` assertion rests on. The Lambda
# image DOES have one, because those same exclusions would leave its build with no source at all.
#
# A .env reaching the build context is a secret leak that no test of the built image can see: the
# runtime stage copies only dist/, so anything that leaks in is invisible downstream and permanent
# upstream. The build stage asserts these are absent for that reason.

.git
.github
.claude
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
infra
lambdas
docs
**/dist
**/coverage
htmlcov
**/__pycache__
**/.next
